  "note": "POWER-DOWN SEQUENCING, first ever capture of this. 5 kS/s x 32767 = 6.55 s window (102ms pre, 6451ms post) at 200us resolution. Trigger = VDDIO (V18_P26, ch1) FALLING. Armed with the iPod RUNNING and the SCREEN AWAKE so VDDIO is high and a falling edge is possible; a previous attempt failed because the iPod had already died on low battery. Charger DISCONNECTED (finding 11, and a charging iPod will not power down cleanly). Intended stop: Rockbox software shutdown via Play/Pause. BEWARE: if the panel slept before the shutdown this may have triggered on a SCREEN-SLEEP VDDIO drop instead - check whether the 3.0V rail and the reference also fall, and whether traffic resumes afterwards, before labelling this a shutdown. CAVEAT: rails DECAY rather than switch hard, so a ~1.1V threshold crossing conflates switch-off order with RC decay constants; this shows what the PANEL EXPERIENCES, not necessarily the PMU's switching order.",
